We follow her for half an hour as the wind rises to a gale. Lightning splits the canopy, and the sky opens in a torrential deluge. Within seconds, water pours off our shoulders in sheets, driven sideways by gusts that sting like thrown gravel. The treetops groan and thrash like breaking masts.

"Tighten up!" Daren shouts over the howling wind. "Watch for lightning strikes! Stay under the tallest cover and do not take to the air! Keep moving!"

A crack echoes through the timber as an uprooted pine crashes down fifty paces ahead, sending moss and splintered branches flying. We skirt the debris and press on.

For twenty grueling minutes, we march into the teeth of the gale. Thunder detonates overhead with the force of siege spells, rattling teeth in jaws. The wind pushes hard enough to halt a step mid-stride, and the rain turns the forest floor into a churning torrent of mud.

